{%- comment -%}
  Product card — the photograph.

  Every photograph the piece has is a slide, however many that is, and only the
  first two are fetched up front. That is `snippets/card-slide.liquid`'s rule
  and the reason a slide is `opacity: 0` rather than `display: none`; see
  "Product card" in CLAUDE.md before changing anything here.

  The arrows, the spin badge and the sold-out/sale badge stay **inside** this
  block rather than becoming blocks of their own, and that is structural rather
  than a judgement about how much a merchant should be able to remove:
  `.card__arrow` is `position: absolute; top: 50%`, so its containing block has
  to be `.card__media`. Lifted out to be a sibling it would centre itself on
  the whole card — the caption included — and sit over the price.

  **Every setting the photograph obeys is this block's own** — the frame, the
  fit, the framing correction and whether a spin counts as a slide. They were
  `settings.card_*` under Theme settings → Product cards, read here through an
  `inherit` sentinel; they are stated outright now, so the card is edited where
  the card is rather than in two places.

  The theme settings stay, because `snippets/product-card.liquid` still renders
  the collection and search grids and still reads them. They are not a fallback
  for this block: nothing here consults them, and changing one moves those two
  grids and leaves Most Loved where it is. That is the price of one card built
  two ways, and it ends when those templates are rebuilt on blocks.

  The shipped defaults are the theme settings' own, so the conversion moved no
  pixel — Square and "Fit the whole piece", which is itself a documented
  departure from the design's 3/4 frame.

  The order is the product's own. The metal control deliberately does not touch
  it: "Colour is chosen on the card itself: the name, the price and what goes
  in the bag all follow it. The photograph does not — we shoot one metal."
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product

  assign img_loading = 'lazy'
  assign img_sizes = '(max-width: 700px) 70vw, 460px'

  comment
    Every value has to do what it says, `adapt` included — it fell through to
    the same 3/4 box once, so choosing it changed nothing at all. Adapt takes
    the shape from the first photograph the card actually shows; a card with no
    photograph keeps 3/4, there being nothing to adapt to.
  endcomment
  assign ratio_setting = block.settings.image_ratio

  assign ratio_value = '3 / 4'
  if ratio_setting == 'adapt'
    assign ratio_media = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image' | first
    if ratio_media.width > 0 and ratio_media.height > 0
      assign ratio_value = ratio_media.width | append: ' / ' | append: ratio_media.height
    endif
  else
    assign ratio_value = ratio_setting | replace: '/', ' / '
  endif

  assign fit_value = block.settings.image_fit

  comment
    The design's framing correction. Its photographs are shot on white with
    margins that differ by category, so each needs a different amount cropped
    away for the piece to fill the frame. Matched on type then title, earrings
    before rings because "earrings" contains "ring". A custom.card_zoom
    metafield overrides it per piece; the theme setting turns it off.
  endcomment
  assign card_zoom = blank
  if block.settings.image_zoom
    assign card_zoom = product.metafields.custom.card_zoom.value
    if card_zoom == blank
      assign zoom_match = product.type | append: ' ' | append: product.title | downcase
      assign card_zoom = 1.15
      if zoom_match contains 'bracelet'
        assign card_zoom = 1.05
      elsif zoom_match contains 'earring'
        assign card_zoom = 1.39
      elsif zoom_match contains 'ring'
        assign card_zoom = 1.32
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign card_images = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'
  assign photo_count = card_images.size

  comment
    The spin counts only once an mp4 rendition is known to exist. Counting the
    video itself put the arrows and the badge on a card whose video has none —
    controls for a slide that is never rendered, because the slide is guarded
    on the rendition and the count was not.
  endcomment
  assign card_video = blank
  assign card_mp4 = blank
  if block.settings.show_video
    assign product_videos = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'video'
    assign first_video = product_videos.first
    if first_video != blank
      assign mp4_sources = first_video.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4'
      assign card_mp4 = mp4_sources.last
      if card_mp4 != blank
        assign card_video = first_video
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign slide_count = photo_count
  if card_video != blank
    assign slide_count = slide_count | plus: 1
  endif

  comment
    Slide 0 is what the card shows and slide 1 is what hover previews. Those
    two are the whole of it without scripting, so those two are what the
    browser fetches.
  endcomment
  assign eager_slides = 2
-%}

<div
  class="card__media"
  style="aspect-ratio: {{ ratio_value }};{% if card_zoom != blank %} --card-zoom: {{ card_zoom }};{% endif %} --card-fit: {{ fit_value }};"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if product == blank -%}
    {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
  {%- elsif slide_count > 0 -%}
    {%- assign slide_i = 0 -%}

    {%- for media in card_images -%}
      {%- assign slide_eager = false -%}
      {%- if slide_i < eager_slides -%}
        {%- assign slide_eager = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {% render 'card-slide',
        media: media,
        index: slide_i,
        eager: slide_eager,
        product: product,
        sizes: img_sizes,
        loading: img_loading
      %}
      {%- assign slide_i = slide_i | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- if card_video != blank -%}
      {%- assign card_video_lqip = card_video.preview_image | image_url: width: 40 -%}
      <span
        class="card__slide{% if photo_count == 0 %} is-on{% endif %}"
        data-card-slide="{{ photo_count }}"
        data-card-spin
      >
        <video
          class="card__img card__video"
          data-src="{{ card_mp4.url }}"
          poster="{{ card_video.preview_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
          width="{{ card_video.preview_image.width | default: 1240 }}"
          height="{{ card_video.preview_image.height | default: 827 }}"
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          preload="none"
          aria-label="{{ 'products.spin_view' | t }}"
          data-video-lqip="{{ card_video_lqip }}"
        ></video>
        {% render 'video-lqip-frame', lqip: card_video_lqip %}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="card__slide is-on">
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if card_video != blank -%}
    <span class="card__spin" data-card-spin-label{% if photo_count > 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
      {{- 'products.spin_badge' | t -}}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if slide_count > 1 -%}
    <button
      class="card__arrow card__arrow--prev"
      type="button"
      data-card-step="-1"
      data-tip="{{ 'products.previous_view' | t }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'products.previous_view' | t }}"
    >
      <svg width="10" height="20" viewBox="0 0 12 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M10 2L2 12l8 10" />
      </svg>
    </button>
    <button
      class="card__arrow card__arrow--next"
      type="button"
      data-card-step="1"
      data-tip="{{ 'products.next_view' | t }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'products.next_view' | t }}"
    >
      <svg width="10" height="20" viewBox="0 0 12 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M2 2l8 10-8 10" />
      </svg>
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if product != blank -%}
    {%- if product.available == false -%}
      <span class="badge">{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}</span>
    {%- elsif product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
      <span class="badge">{{ 'products.on_sale' | t }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_image.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "t:sections.all.image_ratio.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.adapt" },
        { "value": "1/1", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.square" },
        { "value": "4/5", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.portrait" },
        { "value": "3/4", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.tall_portrait" },
        { "value": "4/3", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.landscape" }
      ],
      "default": "1/1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_fit",
      "label": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_image_fit.label",
      "info": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_image_fit.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "contain", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.contain" },
        { "value": "cover", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.cover" }
      ],
      "default": "contain"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "image_zoom",
      "label": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_image_zoom.label",
      "info": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_image_zoom.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_video",
      "label": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_show_video.label",
      "info": "t:settings_schema.product_cards.card_show_video.info",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_image.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
